9\n\n--- Record 502 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: 28039\n\n--- Record 503 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.43.1\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Logs: Besides FluentBit, you can now also use OTLP as output for you LogPipeline resources. Based on an OTel Collector, you can tail logs from stdout/stderr, as well as push logs from applications. The gateway enriches your log data in the same way as for traces and metrics. For details, see Application Logs (#556).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: For all your pipelines using an OTLP output, you can centrally configure enriching the data with Pod labels, so that the data gets k8s.pod.label.label attributes. For details, see Data Enrichment (#2195).      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.128.0 (#2221).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 504 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Corrected Condition Base Calculation for Conditions with Multiple Counters\nDescription: When a condition had multiple counters and the step number was set to zero for that condition, the condition base incorrectly included results from subsequent steps. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 505 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Validation Fix for Zero-Value Conditions in Price Agreement\nDescription: When a condition was passed with a value of 0.000 and the plus/minus flag was set to negative in the condition type customizing, it incorrectly triggered a validation error in the Price agreement scenario. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 506 ---\nComponent: Personalized Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code, stability, and performance improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 507 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.14\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data marketplace, data modeling, data privacy and protection, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.14. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 508 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Centers\nDescription: The Responsibility Management Service is now also available in the following regions:  AWS: EU12 - Europe (Frankfurt)  Google Cloud Platform: US30 - US Central (IA)  Google Cloud Platform: EU30 - Europe (Frankfurt)  See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-14\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 509 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use a new function, TRUNC in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 510 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availibility of the Externalization feature on Edge Integration Cell\nDescription: You can now use the externalization feature to define API policies that can retrieve externalized configuration values during runtime. These parameters can be utilized later without modifying the standard API artifact. For more information, see Externalize Parameter for API Artifact.\n", "07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 510 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availibility of the Externalization feature on Edge Integration Cell\nDescription: You can now use the externalization feature to define API policies that can retrieve externalized configuration values during runtime. These parameters can be utilized later without modifying the standard API artifact. For more information, see Externalize Parameter for API Artifact.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-06\nValid as Of: 2025-07-06\nVersion: 2505\n\n", "--- Record 1411 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Communication Management: Local APIs\nDescription: The communication management will provide local APIs for the creation and update of communication arrangements, communication systems, communication users, and the upload of client certificates.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1412 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations App: Title Name Change\nDescription: When a business configuration object is selected, the application title now changes to the name of the business configuration object.See Custom Business Configurations App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1413 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Integration Using SQL Service\nDescription: The documentation Accessing ABAP-Managed Data Using SQL Services for Data Integration Scenarios has moved to a central guide dedicated to integration and connectivity. You can find all information relating to accessing ABAP-managed data using SQL services in the chapters about data integration: ABAP Integration and Connectivity: Data Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1414 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Developing Inbound and Outbound Communication\nDescription: The documentation Developing External Service Consumption (Outbound Communication) and Developing APIs for Inbound Communication has been moved to a central guide dedicated to integration and connectivity. You can find all information relating to inbound and outbound communication in the chapters about process integration: ABAP Integration and Connectivity: Process Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1415 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Editable Treeview with Draft Capabilities\nDescription: In RAP, a treeview visualizes data modeled by a CDS hierarchy, using an SAP Fiori Elements treetable. Previously, you could model hierarchical structures and expose them as read-only treeviews to the SAP Fiori UI. Now you can also expose hierarchical structures as editable treeviews with draft capabilities.   For more information, see Treeviews and Editable Treeviews with Draft Capabilities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1416 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Event-Driven Side Effects\nDescription: You can now define an event to trigger a side effect in your RAP business object. Whenever a defined event is raised by the application server, the side effect is triggered and the defined targets are reloaded.   For more information, see Event-Driven RAP Side Effects\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1417 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Export Customizing Transports: Release All\nDescription: You can now release all open customizing requests at once.See Working in the Export Customizing Transports App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1418 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Harmonized Context Menu in Key User Adaptation\nDescription: The context menu is now consistent when you select elements. It no longer depends on how you select an element, such as using the left or right mouse button. The familiar right-click context menu now also appears when you left-click an element.  For more information, see Making UI Changes (Object Pages).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1419 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hide Empty Spaces and Pages in the SAP Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: Spaces and pages are not shown when they are empty because of the user's role context. This feature is opt-in, so it's disabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES  is set to the default value false that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Note  SAP plans to activate this feature by default with the upcoming 2505 SAP BTP ABAP environment release. You can now try it out and inform your users, if necessary, about a potential change of behavior.With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from", " feature is opt-in, so it's disabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES  is set to the default value false that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. Note  SAP plans to activate this feature by default with the upcoming 2505 SAP BTP ABAP environment release. You can now try it out and inform your users, if necessary, about a potential change of behavior.With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from the Manage Launchpad Settings app, and empty spaces and pages will continue to be hidden by default.  For more information, see Empty Spaces and Pages Not Displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1420 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: How to Display Open Transport Requests\nDescription: You can now display open transport requests by searching a table in the Manage Software Components app.  For more information, see Display Open Transport Requests.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n", "--- Record 2301 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes to Metering and Pricing for Premium Edition\nDescription: The field count used in calculating prices for blocks for 100 for SAP Document AI now includes categories added to a schema. Each category is counted as one field.  See Blocks of 100 Documents for Premium Edition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-09\nValid as Of: 2024-09-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2302 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Combine Different Setup Types for Line Items in Schema (Premium Edition)\nDescription: With SAP Document AI you can now use different extraction methods for line item fields in the same schema. Formerly, this was possible only for header fields.  See Setup Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-09\nValid as Of: 2024-09-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2303 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Certification of MySQL 8.0\nDescription: MySQL 8.0 has been certified for use as a source in tasks/dataflows. For more information, see the Product Availability Matrix (PAM).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-06\nValid as Of: 2024-09-06\nVersion: 1.0.11.54\n\n--- Record 2304 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Clarification about OData V2 Function Import and AUTO OData Version\nDescription: The help topics OData Adapter Options and Importing OData function operations have been updated to state that when OData Version is set to AUTO, function import is not supported.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-01\nValid as Of: 2024-09-06\nVersion: 1.0.11.54\n\n--- Record 2305 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: New Field for DB2 iSeries Datastores\nDescription: For DB2 iSeries 7.4 certification, a new Additional connection information field has been added when creating a DB2 iSeries datastore configuration. For more information, see DB2.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-01\nValid as Of: 2024-09-06\nVersion: 1.0.11.54\n\n--- Record 2306 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Release Update\nDescription: We've made performance-related improvements in this release. No new features have been added.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-06\nValid as Of: 2024-09-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2307 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: General Availability of SAP S/4HANA Public Cloud Extensibility Wizard\nDescription: You can now use the SAP S/4HANA Public Cloud Extensibility wizard to easily create on-stack extensions like custom fields and custom logic. You can also use the wizard to develop side-by-side extensions such as custom processes in SAP Build Process Automation.  See Using the Extensibility Wizard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-06\nValid as Of: 2024-09-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2308 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Command in the SAP AI Core Catalog\nDescription: You can further utilize the generative AI capabilities by using the new GenerateGpt4OmniCompletion command from the provided SAP AI Core (aicore-sapcp) catalog. See GenerateGpt4OmniCompletion Command.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-05\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2309 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: HTML5 Business Solutions – Multitenancy Support\nDescription: Building on our recent introduction of HTML5 Business Solutions as a Content Provider, cross subaccount access of multitenant business solutions is now supported.  With this enhancement, HTML5 business solutions that expose CDM content can now be accessed from their subscription subaccount. These multitenant solutions, once subscribed to from a subaccount, can be configured as content providers in the Cloud Portal instance.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-05\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: 2408B\n\n--- Record 2310 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Transparent Proxy for Kubernetes - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Transparent Proxy version 1.6.0 provides the following bug fixes:      Fixed an issue with incorrectly parsed dots in the Address field of SAP BTP", " Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-05\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: 2408B\n\n--- Record 2310 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Transparent Proxy for Kubernetes - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Transparent Proxy version 1.6.0 provides the following bug fixes:      Fixed an issue with incorrectly parsed dots in the Address field of SAP BTP destinations of type TCP. You can now define addresses without any character limitation.   For more information, see TCP Destinations.      Fixed multiple Golang vulnerabilities by upgrading dependencies to a newer version.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-05\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_43f0d7636fdc1712cbd82accd3360e2a5bc169b008f90f01730c8843bb68fa95_v2"}